> I've tried googling for this, but no luck so far.  Is there a patch
> out there for OS/8 V3Q RESORC.SV to list the IDE and RAM disk devices
> by their names rather than the rather odd "(6775), (6776), X, J4", etc?
> 
> It was easy to find the patch for PIP.SV to be able to zero these
> devices, but I can't seem to find a patch for RESORC (and I think
> I remember finding it, long ago when my SBC6120 was new).

I had no luck with either Google or my own archives, but looking at 
RESORC.PA, it looks like this would be pretty simple.  There's a table 
at 02000 that is supposed to describe the devices, and the octal stuff 
is what you get if the first word of a table entry is zero.  Each table 
entry is 4 words long, so...

Device 43 goes at location 02214:
 2615 / DEVICE VM01
 6061
 5300 / size (-1344)
 0000 / no special routine

Device 44 goes at location 02220:
 1104 / DEVICE ID01
 6061
 0001 / size (-4095)
 0000 / no special routine

These locations should be zeroes before the patch is applied.

I'm not really sure what the special routine buys you, but I 
think it lets you print extra device specific magic like the 
unit number.

If you want to print just the unit number, QTC08 will do just 
that.  If you examine location 02073, it will give you the 
address of QTC08, which you can then use instead of the zeroes 
above.

I haven't tried it yet, so back up your RESORC first :-).

Hope it helps!

